@prefix gmeow:   <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/> .
@prefix rdfs:    <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#> .
@prefix skos:    <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#> .
@prefix dcterms: <http://purl.org/dc/terms/> .

<https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/slices/work-orchestration>
    a gmeow:Slice ;
    rdfs:label "work-orchestration"@x-gmeow-english ;
    skos:definition "The work-orchestration slice (core tier): the DOMAIN BINDING of the general prescription/enactment/commitment kernel onto continuing work. The kernel in `logic:` is domain-neutral by construction — it is declared standalone and takes no axiom edge into `gmeow:`, so that one algebra can serve a workflow, a DAG, a repeatable guide, a curriculum, a control plan and an organizational guide alike. This slice is where the durable-work reading of it gets its `gmeow:`-typed edges: a gmeow:WorkCluster binds a continuing goal, a governing gmeow:Norm, a gmeow:EventSchedule recurrence, an active logic:PrescriptionVersion, a versioned gmeow:GuidanceSet and retained gmeow:Note working memory; the derived frontier reaches the preference apparatus through gmeow:CandidateSet and gmeow:ComparisonContext rather than minting a second recommendation model; and the operator review projection ships as a gmeow:ProjectionReceipt carrying an explicit preservation judgment, because collapsing coexisting standpoint-indexed classifications into one operator view is a real loss and must be disclosed rather than hidden. It is core because durable work orchestration is what GMEOW refuses to make optional: an agent runtime that treats 'did my effect actually commit?' as an add-on has already answered that question badly, by default."@x-gmeow-english ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/slices/work-orchestration> ;
    dcterms:title "GMEOW Work-Orchestration Module"@x-gmeow-english ;
    dcterms:creator "Blackcat Informatics® Inc." ;
    gmeow:sliceTier gmeow:tierCore ;
    gmeow:sliceDependsOn
        <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/slices/kernel> ,
        <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/slices/logic> ,
        <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/slices/math> ,
        <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/slices/teleology> ,
        <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/slices/events> ,
        <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/slices/calendar> ,
        <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/slices/observations> ,
        <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/slices/provenance> ,
        <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/slices/versions> ,
        <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/slices/norms> ,
        <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/slices/notes> ,
        <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/slices/preference> ,
        <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/slices/standpoint> ,
        <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/slices/temporal> ;
    gmeow:sliceConsumer "Project Lillith's durable work organ: continuing maintenance clusters that recur on a schedule, each occurrence a fresh immutable enactment against a closed input generation, resumable across a crash, refining abstract steps into pinned executable subgraphs, and dispatching external effects under exact approval binding with reconciliation rather than blind retry at the boundary. It needs every recommendation attributable and contestable, every blocked action explained, and the operator review surface honest about what it collapsed."@x-gmeow-english .
